  "explanation": "Soil formation requires the conversion of parent material into a mixture of mineral particles and organic matter. The fastest pathway among the options is the biological decomposition of a rotting log, which rapidly adds organic material (humus) and promotes aggregation of mineral particles, creating a nascent soil profile within months to a few years. In contrast, a rock in a garden weathers only very slowly through physical and chemical processes, water in a stream primarily transports existing sediments rather than generating new soil in place, and wave action on a beach redistributes sand without producing the organic‑mineral matrix characteristic of soil. Therefore, the log rotting in a forest will form new soil the fastest.",
